<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Harbor.E2E.Framework: shared infrastructure for all Harbor E2E test projects.

    Provides:
      * IE2eDriver         - common contract for driving a Harbor app from
                             outside the process (start, send input, read screen,
                             wait for text/exit, stop).
      * CliDriver          - Process.Start-based driver for one-shot CLI commands
                             (harbor ask ..., harbor version, etc.).
      * TuiDriver          - PTY-wrapped driver for interactive TUI renderers
                             (SpectreTui, Termina, Terminal.Gui, RazorConsole).
                             Uses `script -qfc` on Linux/macOS and ConPTY on
                             Windows (Windows impl is stubbed, see notes).
      * MockLlmServer      - in-process OpenAI-compatible HTTP server. Returns
                             canned SSE-streamed chat completions. Thread-safe.
      * E2eTestBase        - TUnit base class. Per-class MockLlmServer + temp HOME.

    Test projects reference this framework + the app project under test, then
    write 3-5 [Category("E2E")] tests each. All E2E tests are filterable via
    `dotnet test -filter "Category=E2E"` so they can run separately from the
    fast unit test suite in CI.

    THIS PROJECT CARRIES NO [Test] METHODS, AND THAT IS A RULE, NOT A COINCIDENCE.

    TUnit discovers the test classes of a REFERENCED test project inside every
    project that references it, so a [Test] method declared here runs once per
    referencing project. StateTestRunnerTests.cs used to live here and therefore
    ran SIX times per CI run (Harbor.E2E.App.Avalonia, Harbor.E2E.Cli,
    Harbor.LoadTests, Harbor.Tui.E2E.Tests, Harbor.Tui.CellForge.PtyTests and
    Harbor.Ipc.Tests) — 156 executions of 26 tests. The tests now live in
    tests/Harbor.E2E.Framework.Tests, a project nothing references, so they run
    exactly once.

    WHAT THE FRAMEWORK'S OWN TESTS COVER NOW (issue #1812)

    The 26 tests that moved out of here in #1943 asserted on StateTestRunner,
    and StateTestRunner had no consumer: the state-based E2E harness it was
    written for was never wired to a scenario, so the 26 tests were green and
    guarded nothing. StateTestRunner is gone (495 lines), and the framework's
    tests now cover the helpers the OTHER five E2E projects depend on at run
    time: the ANSI scrubber (AnsiStripper) and the 2D terminal emulator
    (AnsiTerminalBuffer), which is what every PTY scenario asserts on.

    tests/Harbor.Architecture.Tests/TestProjectReferenceRules.cs enforces both
    halves of that: a test project must not reference another test project
    unless it uses its types, and a test project that another test project
    references must not declare test methods at all.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591;CA1707;S3267;S2365;S2445;S6618;TUnit0055;NU1504</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Harbor.Abstractions\Harbor.Abstractions.csproj"/>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Harbor.Application\Harbor.Application.csproj"/>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Harbor.Ui.Framework\Harbor.Ui.Framework.csproj"/>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- CE-5 Зона 1: PtySession/AnsiTerminalBuffer internals for the PTY scenario suite. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Harbor.Tui.CellForge.PtyTests"/>
    <!--
      The framework's own unit tests (#1812). AnsiStripper and
      AnsiTerminalBuffer are internal, and the tests are about them, so the
      edge has to be declared: without it the test project could not name the
      types it is about.
    -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Harbor.E2E.Framework.Tests"/>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
